1
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:06,480
You don't want the borders
opened either, do you?

2
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:08,380
You can be honest with me.

3
00:00:11,180 --> 00:00:12,010
After all,

4
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:14,137
you were desperate enough
to go to a pirate to

5
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:16,985
buy the weapons you needed
to fight their kind.

6
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:23,040
It's almost as if
everything's a big joke, Tom.

7
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:31,480
You must be hurting after
the loss of your arms broker,

8
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:35,800
Dothamingo, and now with
your veil of anonymity gone,

9
00:00:36,140 --> 00:00:39,500
you have no choice but
to deal with us directly.

10
00:00:41,260 --> 00:00:46,480
You do realize we have the upper hand
when you're in a position like that.

11
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:50,753
You really shouldn't be making
such unreasonable demands.

12
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:52,880
You've seen Wano, yes?

13
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:56,266
We're as self-sufficient
as they come, friend.

14
00:01:01,420 --> 00:01:03,880
The people of Wano look awfully happy.

15
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:05,977
I'm sure you've noticed that yourselves.

16
00:01:06,060 --> 00:01:08,477
Although there's one thing
we're always in need of,

17
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:10,560
and that's more power in my hands.

18
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:13,280
My request was a warship before.

19
00:01:15,280 --> 00:01:18,480
But now, we demand Dr. Vegapunk!

20
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:21,820
No, we can't!

21
00:01:26,040 --> 00:01:29,120
I wasn't asking, I'm telling you.

22
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:36,860
Celestial dragons, the navy.

23
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:42,300
You must have caught on by now that the
land of Wano fears none of these things.

24
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:49,897
Even if you pulled your
forces together to attack us.

25
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:52,697
You'd never be able to bring
our nation to its knees.

26
00:01:52,780 --> 00:01:55,337
I have Kaido on my side.

27
00:01:55,420 --> 00:02:02,040
I am unstoppable.

28
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:12,320
One dream, one wish.

29
00:02:12,540 --> 00:02:15,740
If you want it, gotta go over the top.

30
00:02:33,240 --> 00:02:36,400
Setting sail and heading for the unknown.

31
00:02:37,900 --> 00:02:41,020
Cutting through the
winds and waves as I go.

32
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:44,057
Gotta keep it up, never stopping, no.

33
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:46,457
Cause I'm aiming to get there first, yeah.

34
00:02:46,540 --> 00:02:49,037
It's all or nothing, no time to worry.

35
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:51,860
Do it later, right now I'm living free.

36
00:02:55,060 --> 00:02:59,077
When your foes look like
they will overwhelm you.

37
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:03,880
It means your heart's saying
this is what you can't do.

38
00:03:04,920 --> 00:03:07,197
Despite all that to run is not an option.

39
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:09,297
Once they're closed, they
feel the satisfaction.

40
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:11,577
You think I'm rude,
here's my appreciation.

41
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:14,680
When things are getting
tough, just gotta smile.

42
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:19,957
If you are going on your way.

43
00:03:20,040 --> 00:03:22,197
And you're looking for
a fresh, brand new day.

44
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:25,337
Then make sure your only
thought you have is.

45
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:26,797
Yes, I can.

46
00:03:26,880 --> 00:03:31,957
As you're on your way,
marks maps will be made.

47
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:34,920
Yes, with every step that you will take.

48
00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:38,037
Just look at all you've been through.

49
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:40,277
Look ahead to new horizons in view.

50
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:44,480
Shining brightly, oh, who
knows what's waiting for you.

51
00:03:45,560 --> 00:03:47,757
Dream living, that's the way.

52
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:49,817
Make like a hurricane.

53
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:52,860
Now, got to make your mark today.

54
00:03:54,980 --> 00:03:58,797
One dream, one wish.

55
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:00,637
Your dreams don't run away.

56
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:03,617
Go for the knockout.

57
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:05,720
Over the top.

58
00:04:17,180 --> 00:04:19,997
Lady Komurasaki is here.

59
00:04:20,080 --> 00:04:21,500
Make way.

60
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:37,360
I'm late, I know!

61
00:04:40,100 --> 00:04:41,680
You had me worried.

62
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:45,520
Sorry I can't be waiting so long.

63
00:04:45,720 --> 00:04:47,360
Well, let's get to work.

64
00:04:48,080 --> 00:04:48,910
Kay!

65
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:52,330
Ah!

66
00:04:55,940 --> 00:04:58,120
Lady Komonosaki is approaching!

67
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:03,212
The procession's coming!

68
00:05:03,940 --> 00:05:05,540
How much longer?

69
00:05:05,880 --> 00:05:08,617
That's a pretty hefty
crowd she's got riled up.

70
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:10,857
You think she's as pretty as they say?

71
00:05:10,940 --> 00:05:12,260
This is nuts!

72
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:13,500
Hurry up!

73
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:15,420
I can't take it anymore!

74
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:24,500
I hate that bitch!

75
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:26,270
Komurasaki!

76
00:05:27,320 --> 00:05:28,150
Komurasaki!

77
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:30,170
Komurasaki!

78
00:05:32,820 --> 00:05:34,660
Looks like they want trouble.

79
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:37,500
Hey, stop!

80
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:39,020
It's too late now.

81
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:41,260
I have to murder her!

82
00:05:41,620 --> 00:05:44,160
I'm being expelled from the capital.

83
00:05:44,640 --> 00:05:46,720
It's all over for me!

84
00:05:47,220 --> 00:05:49,380
If I'm destined to die anyway,

85
00:05:50,280 --> 00:05:52,000
I'll take her down, too!

86
00:06:01,980 --> 00:06:04,220
Stay away from the Oiran, you trash!

87
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:18,750
Why?

88
00:06:18,833 --> 00:06:20,480
Why would she do this to me?

89
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:26,080
I wish to be by your side forever.

90
00:06:26,940 --> 00:06:28,460
If only it were possible.

91
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:33,157
You want to be with an
old bag of bones like me?

92
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:37,060
If I have no choice but to stay
here as the Shogun's plaything,

93
00:06:37,380 --> 00:06:41,860
then I would much rather have my
contract sold to a kind man such as you.

94
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:46,880
But the price of my freedom is
so steep, I fear it's impossible.

95
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:48,900
Forgive me.

96
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:50,748
I shouldn't have spoken up.

97
00:06:50,880 --> 00:06:55,920
If the Shogun were to hear I said such
a thing, I would surely face his wrath.

98
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:59,000
You must not lose heart, dear.

99
00:06:59,420 --> 00:07:01,937
Would that really bring
you true happiness?

100
00:07:02,020 --> 00:07:05,480
Say the word and I, bingo,
shall make it happen.

101
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:09,460
You would do that for me?

102
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:14,640
I am delighted to hear it,
even if nothing comes to be.

103
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:20,280
What do you mean you can't pay me back?

104
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,540
Forgive us.

105
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:23,820
Do you take me for a fool?

106
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:27,544
Crying won't bail you
out, so just knock it off.

107
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:31,180
I'll take your house as
collateral for the overdue loan.

108
00:07:34,580 --> 00:07:35,940
For you, m 'lady.

109
00:07:36,520 --> 00:07:38,120
That is quite a lot.

110
00:07:38,260 --> 00:07:40,020
I've never seen such wealth.

111
00:07:40,260 --> 00:07:41,260
You can count it.

112
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:45,797
This is going to be the down payment so
that I may buy you from the pleasure hall.

113
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:48,260
It's not enough, but do hold on to it.

114
00:07:48,760 --> 00:07:51,289
Please allow me to mark
this in the ledger.

115
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:53,157
There's no need to bother.

116
00:07:53,240 --> 00:07:56,500
Only a fool would have
distrust in the woman he loves.

117
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:59,000
Your word will do just fine.

118
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:00,620
You're too kind.

119
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:02,860
Thank you.

120
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:05,900
I long for the day we go home together.

121
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:14,080
Don't cry.

122
00:08:14,420 --> 00:08:15,580
I have a solution.

123
00:08:16,860 --> 00:08:19,540
Allow me to organize the funeral for you.

124
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:23,078
I'll front the money until
you get back on your feet.

125
00:08:25,760 --> 00:08:28,060
Stop with the crying already!

126
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:31,805
Oh, don't act surprised
that you owe me double!

127
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:35,060
You shouldn't expect a
favor to come without a fee!

128
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:41,180
Here is your money, my love. Incredible!

129
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:44,560
Though I fear I'd bear ill tidings.

130
00:08:44,780 --> 00:08:46,017
What's wrong, my love?

131
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:48,557
I've heard that another man is interested

132
00:08:48,640 --> 00:08:52,400
in buying my contract and
has put in a bid. Hey, what?

133
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:54,320
There's no time.

134
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:57,037
I need to gather more
money before it's too late.

135
00:08:57,120 --> 00:08:59,100
What else can I sell around here?

136
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:04,280
I sold everything I own, Gomorrah Saki.

137
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:07,400
I'm so lucky to have met you.

138
00:09:08,460 --> 00:09:09,640
Enough already.

139
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,353
That's the final straw.

140
00:09:14,040 --> 00:09:15,660
I'm moving back home.

141
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:17,271
I can't take you anymore.

142
00:09:17,400 --> 00:09:18,760
Do whatever you want.

143
00:09:21,620 --> 00:09:22,920
Oh, darling.

144
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:24,640
Be right there.

145
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:28,900
I've abandoned my family for you.

146
00:09:31,900 --> 00:09:33,600
Oh my, your health.

147
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:35,447
Take care of yourself, dear.

148
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:38,837
Don't you worry about me.

149
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:40,640
I can just tough it out.

150
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:43,040
Medicine is a waste of money.

151
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:45,017
The quicker I can get your payment,

152
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:48,180
the sooner we can live
together happily ever after.

153
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:49,580
Oh my goodness.

154
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,060
I am so lucky to have you.

155
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:55,100
My love, I dream of that day too.

156
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:58,540
Go, Murasaki.

157
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:06,320
The deed is done.

158
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:10,277
I may no longer have a place to live,
but I have all the money in hand.

159
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:11,657
We can build from scratch.

160
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:14,400
This is the final 500 gold coins.

161
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:15,917
You've been patient.

162
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:17,780
The day is finally here.

163
00:10:18,080 --> 00:10:19,080
Let's go home.

164
00:10:21,840 --> 00:10:22,670
What?

165
00:10:23,180 --> 00:10:24,010
Apologies.

166
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:26,960
However, the oiron is unwell today.

167
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:28,631
That's quite unfortunate.

168
00:10:28,880 --> 00:10:31,557
Regardless, please make sure
this gets into her hands.

169
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:32,758
I will return soon.

170
00:10:40,140 --> 00:10:40,970
Komurasaki!

171
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:44,260
I've come to save you
from this wretched life!

172
00:10:44,500 --> 00:10:46,920
You're free to come home with me at last!

173
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:02,040
I can't believe this guy.

174
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,520
Nice going, you old love-struck pervert!

175
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:08,677
All right, all right, everyone.

176
00:11:08,760 --> 00:11:10,777
That's quite enough laughing!

177
00:11:10,860 --> 00:11:11,797
Wrap it up.

178
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:13,140
Now go fetch her.

179
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:17,737
You realize she's expecting me?

180
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:20,526
We have both been looking
forward to this day.

181
00:11:22,980 --> 00:11:23,810
Pathetic.

182
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:26,216
You really believed in all that crap?

183
00:11:26,300 --> 00:11:28,360
She has enough money to free her.

184
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:31,127
I've been saving it up
for a while, actually.

185
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:33,132
Komunasaki's holding it.

186
00:11:34,520 --> 00:11:36,300
Oh, bingo. It's you.

187
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:38,760
Ah, there you are.

188
00:11:39,140 --> 00:11:40,840
I'm delighted to see you.

189
00:11:41,220 --> 00:11:44,457
Why don't you explain our
relationship to these skeptics,

190
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:46,481
as they don't seem to believe me?

191
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:48,497
Yes, of course.

192
00:11:48,580 --> 00:11:54,460
As I recall, our relationship is that
you provide me with money and I keep it.

193
00:11:55,100 --> 00:11:55,930
Huh?

194
00:12:02,900 --> 00:12:04,660
I've already spent it all.

195
00:12:06,520 --> 00:12:07,720
Thank you, though.

196
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:14,637
That old Greg really thought that
Komurasaki fell in love with him?!

197
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:15,550
What a joke!

198
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:28,080
Huh?

199
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:30,320
They're a problem?

200
00:12:30,640 --> 00:12:33,180
Is this geezer bothering you? Huh?

201
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:34,940
Just give me the word.

202
00:12:37,820 --> 00:12:39,400
The boss Kyoshiro.

203
00:12:40,660 --> 00:12:41,920
I see.

204
00:12:42,820 --> 00:12:47,220
So you're the filthy old stalker who's
been harassing Komodosaki lately.

205
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,440
Our love was not fictitious.

206
00:12:50,040 --> 00:12:51,100
Believe me.

207
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:54,520
Please, Komodosaki, tell him the truth.

208
00:12:57,300 --> 00:13:00,620
I beg you, don't tell me
this was all for naught.

209
00:13:00,900 --> 00:13:03,477
The sacrifices I made,
there's nothing left.

210
00:13:03,560 --> 00:13:05,820
I threw away everything I had.

211
00:13:06,060 --> 00:13:07,400
It was all for you.

212
00:13:19,560 --> 00:13:21,580
You're one of many, old-timer.

213
00:13:22,020 --> 00:13:23,640
We can't let you cry here.

214
00:13:23,880 --> 00:13:25,137
It's bad for business.

215
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:26,050
Time to go.

216
00:13:26,420 --> 00:13:28,360
Having some trouble standing up?

217
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:29,520
We can help.

218
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:31,480
Get lost.

219
00:13:31,660 --> 00:13:33,000
You got ripped off.

220
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:40,780
Get on to me.

221
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:43,480
Stop! Please!

222
00:13:44,480 --> 00:13:45,860
Get up now!

223
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:47,580
I'm leaving!

224
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:49,040
I'm sorry!

225
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:02,600
Go, Murasaki!

226
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:14,400
The top Oiran's procession
is coming through!

227
00:14:16,360 --> 00:14:19,460
Make way for her passage!

228
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:26,640
Lady Komurasaki!

229
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:33,620
That's her!

230
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:35,980
Are you guys seeing this too?

231
00:14:41,020 --> 00:14:42,920
She's so beautiful!

232
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:45,160
Whoa, her glove!

233
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:51,510
Kuburasaki!

234
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:55,060
I sold my house and family to be with you!

235
00:14:55,300 --> 00:14:57,580
Give it back to me, you swindler!

236
00:14:57,980 --> 00:15:00,160
I trusted you!

237
00:15:02,180 --> 00:15:04,420
Return the gift you gave to me?

238
00:15:04,940 --> 00:15:06,140
You are pathetic.

239
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:12,920
To me, men are nothing more
than dogs that fetch me riches.

240
00:15:13,520 --> 00:15:16,680
With nothing left to give
me, you are worthless.

241
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:23,580
There's no escaping now.

242
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:27,618
Don't give us trouble, you peasants.

243
00:15:28,820 --> 00:15:32,860
There's no place in the Flower
Capital for you lousy deadbeats.

244
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:36,900
In the name of Shogun Orochi,
we banish you from here!

245
00:15:39,980 --> 00:15:42,100
Please have mercy on me!

246
00:15:42,420 --> 00:15:45,780
None of us are suited for
living outside of the city!

247
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:50,740
Dem you all to hell! Komurasaki!

248
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:56,340
Sorry, your pleas fall upon deaf ears.

249
00:15:57,580 --> 00:15:59,300
I resent the poor.

250
00:16:17,640 --> 00:16:19,740
Open the case!

251
00:16:28,660 --> 00:16:32,800
The Oiran Komurasaki has arrived!

252
00:16:51,020 --> 00:16:53,608
So, you got a little
sister out there, Momo?

253
00:16:54,260 --> 00:16:56,577
Manners Tama, who do you think I am?

254
00:16:56,660 --> 00:16:58,484
You should address me properly.

255
00:16:59,040 --> 00:16:59,870
Your momo.

256
00:17:01,040 --> 00:17:02,180
Just forget it.

257
00:17:03,740 --> 00:17:05,560
Yes, I do have one.

258
00:17:06,380 --> 00:17:08,480
She would be 26 years old now.

259
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:11,697
While some have witnessed
my mother's death,

260
00:17:11,780 --> 00:17:14,133
none have been able to confirm Hiyori's.

261
00:17:15,080 --> 00:17:15,980
She lives!

262
00:17:16,180 --> 00:17:18,237
I have faith my sister's
out there somewhere.

263
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:20,026
I only pray that she is safe.

264
00:17:20,360 --> 00:17:22,257
Well, I hope you get to meet her soon.

265
00:17:22,340 --> 00:17:23,620
I certainly don't.

266
00:17:24,560 --> 00:17:28,560
